From 8efc0857e5362bea93ee188f2f63c1257bea57fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: timfox <timfox@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:15:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] nodes: reset the graph when FLoadGraph fails part-way

FLoadGraph memcpy's the saved CGraph header, which carries
m_fGraphPresent/m_fGraphPointersSet = TRUE.  On a short file or a failed
calloc it returned FALSE with those flags still set and NULL node/sort
arrays; monster AI then called FindNearestNode and dereferenced m_di
(GameCube DSI at c1a1b, 'Couldn't malloc 57 nodes').  Call InitGraph on
the failure path so the level runs without a graph, as when the .nod is
missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/nodes.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/nodes.cpp b/dlls/nodes.cpp
index fe54500b..acf5b78b 100644
--- a/dlls/nodes.cpp
+++ b/dlls/nodes.cpp
@@ -2618,6 +2618,13 @@ int CGraph::FLoadGraph( const char *szMapName )
 ShortFile:
 NoMemory:
 	FREE_FILE( aMemFile );
+	// The header memcpy above loaded m_fGraphPresent/m_fGraphPointersSet as
+	// they were saved (TRUE). A short file or a failed calloc must not leave
+	// the graph marked present with NULL node/sort arrays: FindNearestNode
+	// would walk m_di (DSI at c1a1b when 57 nodes could not be allocated).
+	// InitGraph frees whatever was allocated and clears the flags, so callers
+	// see "no graph" exactly as when the .nod is missing.
+	InitGraph();
 	return FALSE;
 }
 
